      "postID": "632f97eb24056044af4f0a5a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I feel like there's most definitely a case for the quest limit to be 15 MB compressed, and 40 MB uncompressed.\n\nIt's not a huge increase, so it won't shock too many systems at once. It can be revisited later if it's determined that it didn't cause too many issues. Especially given the discontinuation of the Quest 1, it's extra-relevant. \n\nThose extra 5 MB of compression might be the difference between legible text on an avi, or tattoos you can actually distinguish, and strange gray blobs.\n\nPersonally, I'm a PC player, but I try my absolute hardest to make everything I do compatible for Quest players because I somewhat dislike the platform discrimination, but it's definitely very hard. I'm not asking for 75+ toggle avatars to be allowed on quest, but at least give us room for more textures, something.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
